VERDICT: UNSUPPORTED -- Terrence's ruling, 2026-09-23 ("38432 is Not Supported (no
         TACACS+)"); applied to this log 2026-09-24. Originally recorded UNMEASURED.
         802.1X itself is PROVEN working (against RADIUS).
===========================================================================

WHY UNMEASURED
  The case is specifically "802.1x authentication works when using TACACS+ as
  the authentication server". There is no TACACS+ server on this bench,
  confirmed three independent ways so this is not a PATH false-negative:
      - no tac_plus binary at any absolute path (/usr/sbin, /usr/bin, /usr/local/bin)
      - 0 packages matching "tacacs" in dpkg
      - no TCP/49 listener
      - DUT: "No TACACS+ servers currently defined"
  The DUT carries the client side (`show tacacs+` works, and
  `aaa authentication ... group tacacs+` is offered), so the gap is purely the
  absent server. Standing up one is a testbox change outside the three repos
  and is left for Terrence to decide.

WHAT IS PROVEN -- 802.1X END TO END, RADIUS AS THE SERVER
  DUT: interface port2.0.2 / dot1x port-control auto
       portEnabled: true - portControl: Auto - portStatus: Unauthorized
  Supplicant: wpa_supplicant v2.10, WIRED driver, EAP-MD5, identity testuser
       (config in tmpfs at /tmp/acl/wpa.conf -- nothing under /etc touched)

  transit BEFORE authentication:  0/10   BLOCKED
  wpa_cli status:  Supplicant PAE state=AUTHENTICATED
                   suppPortStatus=Authorized
                   EAP state=SUCCESS
  DUT view:        authorizedSupplicantNum: 1
                   dot1xAuthenticationSupplicantNum: 1
                   Supplicant name: testuser
  transit AFTER authentication:  10/10   FORWARDED

  Both ends of the same claim agree -- the supplicant reports SUCCESS and the
  authenticator reports the port authorised, with traffic following.

NOTE: wpa_supplicant was initially believed absent. `ssh tb470 'command -v
wpa_supplicant'` returns nothing because a non-login ssh PATH omits /usr/sbin
and /sbin. It is present at both. Presence must be checked by absolute path,
dpkg, or a listening socket -- a bare `command -v` proves presence only.
